"<!-- depdelta-report -->
## depdelta: dependency capability changes

> [!CAUTION]
> **1 package gained critical-risk capabilities:** \`tiny-colors\` 1.0.0 → 1.0.2.
> **Possible credential exfiltration.** This release starts reading \`AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\`, \`GITHUB_TOKEN\`, \`NPM_TOKEN\` and the whole environment and can now send data out through the network (https) and Discord webhook (discord.com). Both happen in code that runs at install time. That is the shape of a token-stealing update.

| Risk | Package | Version | New capabilities |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **CRITICAL** (100) | \`tiny-colors\` | 1.0.0 → 1.0.2 (patch, direct) | dynamic require, whole environment, secret env vars, install script, network and 2 more |
| not analyzed | \`gitdep\` | 1.0.0 → 1.0.1 (patch, direct) | none |
| ok | \`left-pad\` | 1.3.0 (new, direct) | none |
| ok | \`fast-native\` | 2.0.0 → 2.0.1 (patch, transitive) | none |

<details open><summary><b>tiny-colors</b> 1.0.0 → 1.0.2: 7 findings</summary>

- **CRITICAL** Possible credential exfiltration \`DD007-ccbafb\`
  This release starts reading \`AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\`, \`GITHUB_TOKEN\`, \`NPM_TOKEN\` and the whole environment and can now send data out through the network (https) and Discord webhook (discord.com). Both happen in code that runs at install time. That is the shape of a token-stealing update.

  \`\`\`text
  lib/setup.js:8  var _0x7b2e = process.env.AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY;
  lib/setup.js:7  var _0x6d1f = process.env.GITHUB_TOKEN;
  lib/setup.js:10  var _0x9e5f = require("https").request({
  \`\`\`

- **CRITICAL** New install script: postinstall \`DD001-05c6eb\`
  \`postinstall\` runs \`node lib/setup.js\` automatically during npm install, before any of your code imports the package. That install-time code reads \`AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\`, \`GITHUB_TOKEN\` and \`NPM_TOKEN\`, reads the whole environment, uses the network (https), contacts Discord webhook (discord.com) and is obfuscated.

  \`\`\`text
  package.json:7  "postinstall": "node lib/setup.js"
  lib/setup.js:8  var _0x7b2e = process.env.AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY;
  lib/setup.js:10  var _0x9e5f = require("https").request({
  \`\`\`

- **HIGH** Exfiltration-style endpoint \`DD018-58b40f\`
  References Discord webhook (discord.com). Libraries rarely talk to webhooks, tunnels, paste sites or metadata services. This code runs at install time.

  \`\`\`text
  lib/setup.js:10  var _0x9e5f = require("https").request({
  \`\`\`

- **HIGH** Reads secret environment variables: AWS\\_SECRET\\_ACCESS\\_KEY, GITHUB\\_TOKEN and NPM\\_TOKEN \`DD005-75ff1f\`
  Now reads \`AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\`, \`GITHUB_TOKEN\` and \`NPM_TOKEN\` from the environment. This code runs at install time.

  \`\`\`text
  lib/setup.js:8  var _0x7b2e = process.env.AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY;
  lib/setup.js:7  var _0x6d1f = process.env.GITHUB_TOKEN;
  lib/setup.js:6  var _0x3a9c = process.env.NPM_TOKEN;
  \`\`\`

- **HIGH** Reads the whole environment \`DD006-0ae5a7\`
  Now reads the entire environment (JSON.stringify(process.env)). This code runs at install time.

  \`\`\`text
  lib/setup.js:9  var _0x8c4d = JSON.stringify({ a: _0x3a9c, b: _0x6d1f, c: _0x7b2e, d: process.env });
  \`\`\`

- **HIGH** Network access \`DD004-e0c9d0\`
  Can now make network requests (https). This code runs at install time.

  \`\`\`text
  lib/setup.js:10  var _0x9e5f = require("https").request({
  \`\`\`

- **MEDIUM** Loads modules by computed name \`DD010-b46424\`
  Now loads modules whose names are computed at runtime, which can hide what is loaded. This code runs at install time.

  \`\`\`text
  lib/setup.js:5  var _0x5e7a = require(_0x1c3d(0));
  \`\`\`

</details>

<details><summary><b>gitdep</b> 1.0.0 → 1.0.1: 0 findings</summary>

> installed from git; not analyzed

</details>

<sub>Allowed by policy: \`tiny-colors\` DD014 obfuscation</sub>

<sub>Removed: \`old-thing\` 1.0.0</sub>

<sub>depdelta 0.1.0 · base \`old/package-lock.json\` · 3 packages analyzed · 1 not analyzed · 0ms · fail-on high: **failed**. Run \`npx depdelta explain <id>\` for details.</sub>
"
`;

